# Generic Chapter 1 town NPC.
# A quay bookkeeper who supplies corroboration rather than revelation.
NPC: quay_bookkeeper
LOCATION: waterfront
SCHEDULE: morning=quay_office, midday=quay_office, evening=closed, night=closed

TOPIC: default
  GATE: NOT topic_done(quay_bookkeeper, default) AND coat = plain
  TAG: bookkeeper_plain
  MR. VALE: "The office is closed."
  [He aligns the corner of a loose invoice with the ledger beneath it.]
  MR. VALE: "But you did not come dressed as an office.\n\nWhat are you asking?"

TOPIC: default
  GATE: NOT topic_done(quay_bookkeeper, default)
  TAG: bookkeeper_badge
  MR. VALE: "If this concerns the estate accounts, Officer, the books have already been examined."
  WALTER CORWIN: "By whom?"
  MR. VALE: "By everyone entitled to say they examined them."

TOPIC: work
  GATE: always
  TAG: bookkeeper_work
  LABEL: "Ask what records the office keeps"
  TIME: 3
  WALTER CORWIN: "What passes through these books?"
  MR. VALE: "Freight. Wages. Berthing fees. Repairs when the repair was admitted.\nDebts when the debtor had a name worth writing."
  WALTER CORWIN: "And when the name was not worth writing?"
  MR. VALE: "Then someone generally found a broader word."

TOPIC: unfamiliar_woman
  GATE: evidence(naomi)
  TAG: bookkeeper_naomi
  LABEL: "Ask whether Naomi came to the office"
  TIME: 4
  WALTER CORWIN: "Naomi Freeman. Did she bring that name here?"
  MR. VALE: "A woman brought it.\nWhether the office kept it is a different question."
  WALTER CORWIN: "You remember her."
  MR. VALE: "I remember correcting the clerk who wrote 'inquiry' where she had said 'claim.'"
  NOTEBOOK: bookkeeper_naomi_1 | "A quay-office clerk initially reduced Naomi Freeman's claim to an inquiry. Mr. Vale remembers correcting the entry."
  EVIDENCE: quay_inquiry

TOPIC: old_lay
  GATE: evidence(lay_lead) AND evidence(quay_inquiry)
  TAG: bookkeeper_lay
  LABEL: "Ask how an old whaler's lay would be recorded"
  TIME: 4
  WALTER CORWIN: "If a whaler's lay went unpaid, where would the debt appear?"
  MR. VALE: "In the owner's book first. In the harbor copy if anyone expected an argument.\nIn neither, if everyone who could argue was already at sea."
  WALTER CORWIN: "Could the omission be proved?"
  MR. VALE: "An omission is proved by finding what had to exist on either side of it."
  NOTEBOOK: "An unpaid lay may leave no direct entry.\nSeek adjoining records: crew list, voyage account, owner disbursement, harbor copy."
  EVIDENCE: lay_record_method

TOPIC: estate_freight
  GATE: evidence(service_work)
  TAG: bookkeeper_estate
  LABEL: "Ask about deliveries to the estate"
  TIME: 4
  WALTER CORWIN: "Did the estate receive anything unusual before the deaths?"
  MR. VALE: "Unusual things arrive under ordinary descriptions.\nThat is one purpose of an ordinary description."
  WALTER CORWIN: "Which description?"
  MR. VALE: "Kitchen stone. Two carts billed.\nThree crossed the quay."
  NOTEBOOK: bookkeeper_estate_1 | "Estate freight discrepancy: two carts of kitchen stone billed, three observed crossing the quay."
  EVIDENCE: estate_freight

TOPIC: missing_cart
  GATE: evidence(estate_freight)
  TAG: bookkeeper_missing_cart
  LABEL: "Press him about the third cart"
  TIME: 7
  FORK:
    CHOICE: "Put the discrepancy in writing."
      MR. VALE: "It already was."
      WALTER CORWIN: "Then show me."
      MR. VALE: "I said it was written.\nI did not say the writing was kept."
      NOTEBOOK: bookkeeper_cart_destroyed | "A record of the estate's third freight cart existed but is no longer retained at the quay office."
      EVIDENCE: cart_record_missing
    CHOICE: "Tell me who signed for it."
      MR. VALE: "No one signed."
      WALTER CORWIN: "Three carts crossed without a receiving name?"
      MR. VALE: "One did.\nThat is why I remember the number."
      NOTEBOOK: bookkeeper_cart_unsigned | "The unbilled third cart crossed without a receiving signature. Mr. Vale remembers the procedural exception."
      EVIDENCE: cart_unsigned

TOPIC: records
  GATE: evidence(quay_inquiry) AND NOT topic_done(quay_bookkeeper, records)
  TAG: bookkeeper_records
  LABEL: "Ask why records disappear"
  MR. VALE: "Records do not disappear as often as people say."
  WALTER CORWIN: "What happens to them?"
  MR. VALE: "One clerk files a paper under the ship. Another looks under the owner.\nA third decides the matter was never properly submitted."
  MR. VALE: "By the time anyone calls it missing, every hand involved has done something defensible."
  NOTEBOOK: bookkeeper_records_1 | "The quay office does not require a deliberate falsification to lose a record. Separate defensible filing decisions can make a fact practically unrecoverable."

TOPIC: coat
  GATE: coat = plain AND evidence(quay_inquiry) AND NOT topic_done(quay_bookkeeper, coat)
  TAG: bookkeeper_coat
  LABEL: "Ask why he answered without the badge"
  MR. VALE: "A badge requires an answer that can survive being repeated."
  WALTER CORWIN: "And this coat?"
  MR. VALE: "That coat permits a man to remember what no office is prepared to certify."